|passage=The great '''China''', whose [[king|kyng]] is thought... the greatest prince in the [[world]]e.}}
#* {{RQ:Twain Huckleberry Finn|passage=If he tells them to build a palace forty miles long, out of di'monds, and fill it full of chewing gum, or whatever you want, and fetch an emperor's daughter from '''China''' for you to marry, they've got to do it—and they've got to do it before sun-up next morning, too.}}
#* {{quote-book |en |year=1987 |author=Geoffrey Marston |chapter=Abandonment of Territorial Claims: The Cases of Bouvet and Spratly Islands |title=The British Year Book of International Law 1986 |url=https://archive.org/details/britishyearbooko0057unse/ |volume=57 |location=[[Oxford]] |publisher=w:Clarendon Press |ISBN=0-19-825604-3 |OCLC=657935864 |page=356 |pageurl=https://archive.org/details/britishyearbooko0057unse/page/356/ |passage=The Commissioner General asked for Foreign Office guidance in view of his information about earlier events relating to the British claim. In reply, the Foreign Office, in a telegram dated 12 June 1956, pointed out that as there was now a territorial dispute involving the two '''Chinas''', the Philippines and possibly Vietnam over the Nansha Islands the British vessel should ‘stay well clear’ of Spratly Island.}}
#* {{quote-book |en |url=https://archive.org/details/worldtransformed00bush/ |year=1998 |author=w:George H. W. Bush; et al. |title=w:A World Transformed |location=[[New York]] |publisher=w:Alfred A. Knopf |ISBN=0-679-43248-5 |page=93 |pageurl=https://archive.org/details/worldtransformed00bush/page/93/ |passage=After I was nominated to the vice-presidency, {{w|Ronald Reagan}} asked me to go to '''China''' to reassure {{w|Deng Xiaoping|Deng}} that, despite having mentioned it in a campaign speech, he did not believe in two '''Chinas''', and that he would honor the {{w|Shanghai Communiqué}}—which declared, in effect, that there was but {{w|One China Policy|one '''China'''}}. Joined by his top foreign policy team, Deng listened carefully as I explained that Reagan’s statement had been taken out of context. Just as I was finishing, a door opened and a message was passed down the line of advisors until it reached Deng. On reading it, he looked puzzled and annoyed. “He did it again!” he announced. “Ronald Reagan has again referred to ‘two '''Chinas'''’ in a speech!” I talked fast and got out of there. }}
# {{senseid|en|Q148}} {{place|en|large country|r/East Asia|occupying the region around the [[Yellow River|Yellow]], [[Yangtze]], and [[Pearl]] [[river|Rivers]]}}; the [[People's Republic of China]], since 1949.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 6 1971|title=A Size-up of President Nixon: Interview with Mike Mansfield, Senate Democratic Leader|journal=US News & World Report|page=61
|passage='Only a Nixon' Could Go to '''China'''}}
#* '''2017''', {{w|Donald J. Trump}}, [[s:Remarks by President Trump at Make America Great Again Rally, Harrisburg, PA|speech]] at Make America Great Again Rally, Harrisburg, PA
#*: And I met with the President of '''China''' at great length in Florida, and we had long, long talks&mdash;hours and hours and hours.
#: {{ux|en|'''China''' is 75 years old as of {{w|Chinese National Day|October 1}}, 2024}}
